(a) the K_4-free maximum, my own exhaustive check
    n = 4: exhaustive maximum 5, floor(n^2/3) = 5, T(n,3) has 5 edges -> agree
    n = 5: exhaustive maximum 8, floor(n^2/3) = 8, T(n,3) has 8 edges -> agree
    n = 6: exhaustive maximum 12, floor(n^2/3) = 12, T(n,3) has 12 edges -> agree
    n = 7: exhaustive maximum 16, floor(n^2/3) = 16, T(n,3) has 16 edges -> agree
    n = 8: exhaustive maximum 21, floor(n^2/3) = 21, T(n,3) has 21 edges -> agree
    n = 9: exhaustive maximum 27, floor(n^2/3) = 27, T(n,3) has 27 edges -> agree
    for the range in use the construction side is checked directly:
      T(n,3) has exactly floor(n^2/3) edges for every 10 <= n <= 59: yes

